#: isaaclab.sim.utils.stage.use_stage:3 of
msgid ""
"This function binds the stage to the thread-local context for the "
"duration of the context manager. During the context manager, any call to "
":func:`get_current_stage` will return the stage specified in the context "
"manager. After the context manager is exited, the stage is restored to "
"the default stage attached to the USD context."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.stage.use_stage:8 of
msgid ""
"This function is available in Isaac Sim 5.0 and later. For backwards "
"compatibility, it falls back to a no-op context manager in Isaac Sim < "
"5.0."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.stage.use_stage:12 of
msgid "The stage to set in the context."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.stage.use_stage:14 of
msgid "A context manager that sets the stage in the context."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.stage.use_stage:16 of
msgid "If the stage is not a USD stage instance."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.stage.update_stage:3 of
msgid ""
"This function triggers a single update cycle of the application "
"interface, which in turn updates the stage and all associated systems "
"(rendering, physics, etc.). This is necessary to ensure that changes made"
" to the stage are properly processed and reflected in the simulation."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.stage.update_stage:10 of
msgid ""
"This function calls the application update interface rather than directly"
" updating the stage because the stage update is part of the broader "
"application update cycle that includes rendering, physics, and other "
"systems."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.stage.save_stage:3 of
msgid "If the file already exists, it will be overwritten."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.stage.save_stage:5 of
msgid "The file path to save the current stage to"
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.stage.save_stage:6 of
msgid "Whether to open the saved USD file in place. Defaults to True."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.stage.save_stage:11 of
msgid "When layer creation or save operation fails."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.stage.close_stage:5 of
msgid ""
"Once the stage is closed, it is necessary to open a new stage or create a"
" new one in order to work on it."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.stage.close_stage:8 of
msgid ""
"A callback function to call while closing the stage. The function should "
"take two arguments: a boolean indicating whether the stage is closing and"
" a string indicating the error message if the stage closing fails. "
"Defaults to None, in which case the stage will be closed without a "
"callback."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.stage.close_stage:31 of
msgid "Example with callback function:"
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.stage.clear_stage:3 of
msgid ""
"The function will delete all prims in the stage that satisfy the "
"predicate. If the predicate is None, a default predicate will be used "
"that deletes all prims. The default predicate deletes all prims that are "
"not the root prim, are not under the /Render namespace, have the "
"``no_delete`` metadata, are not ancestral to any other prim, and are not "
"hidden in the stage window."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.stage.clear_stage:8 of
msgid ""
"A user defined function that takes the USD prim as an argument and "
"returns a boolean indicating if the prim should be deleted. If the "
"predicate is None, a default predicate will be used that deletes all "
"prims."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.stage.is_stage_loading:3 of
msgid "True if loading, False otherwise"
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.stage.get_current_stage:3 of
msgid ""
"True to get the fabric stage. False to get the USD stage. Defaults to "
"False."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.stage.get_current_stage:5 of
msgid "The USD or Fabric stage as specified by the input arg fabric."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.stage.get_current_stage_id:3 of
msgid "The current open stage id."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.stage.attach_stage_to_usd_context:3 of
msgid ""
"This function should be called during or after scene is created and "
"before stage is simulated or rendered. If the stage is not in memory or "
"rendering is not enabled, this function will return without attaching."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.stage.attach_stage_to_usd_context:6 of
msgid ""
"This function is available in Isaac Sim 5.0 and later. For backwards "
"compatibility, it returns without attaching to the USD context."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.stage.attach_stage_to_usd_context:10 of
msgid ""
"Whether to attach the stage to the usd context before stage is created. "
"Defaults to False."
msgstr ""

