#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.standardize_xform_ops:3 of
msgid ""
"This function converts a prim's transform stack to use the standard USD "
"transform operation order: [translate, orient, scale]. The function "
"performs the following operations:"
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.standardize_xform_ops:6 of
msgid "Validates that the prim is Xformable"
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.standardize_xform_ops:7 of
msgid "Captures the current local transform (translation, rotation, scale)"
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.standardize_xform_ops:8 of
msgid "Resolves and bakes unit scale conversions (xformOp:scale:unitsResolve)"
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.standardize_xform_ops:9 of
msgid "Creates or reuses standard transform operations (translate, orient, scale)"
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.standardize_xform_ops:10 of
msgid "Sets the transform operation order to [translate, orient, scale]"
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.standardize_xform_ops:11 of
msgid "Applies the preserved or user-specified transform values"
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.standardize_xform_ops:13 of
msgid ""
"The entire modification is performed within an ``Sdf.ChangeBlock`` for "
"optimal performance when processing multiple prims."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.standardize_xform_ops:17 of
msgid ""
"**Standard Transform Order:** The function enforces the USD best practice"
" order: ``xformOp:translate``, ``xformOp:orient``, ``xformOp:scale``. "
"This order is compatible with most USD tools and workflows, and uses "
"quaternions for rotation (avoiding gimbal lock issues)."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.standardize_xform_ops:23 of
msgid ""
"**Pose Preservation:** By default, the function preserves the prim's "
"local transform (relative to its parent). The world-space position of the"
" prim remains unchanged unless explicit ``translation``, ``orientation``,"
" or ``scale`` values are provided."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.standardize_xform_ops:28 of
msgid ""
"**Animation Data Loss:** This function only preserves transform values at"
" the default time code (``Usd.TimeCode.Default()``). Any animation or "
"time-sampled transform data will be lost. Use this function during asset "
"import or preparation, not on animated prims."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.standardize_xform_ops:33 of
msgid ""
"**Unit Scale Resolution:** If the prim has a "
"``xformOp:scale:unitsResolve`` attribute (common in imported assets with "
"unit mismatches), it will be baked into the scale and removed. For "
"example, a scale of (1, 1, 1) with unitsResolve of (100, 100, 100) "
"becomes a final scale of (100, 100, 100)."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.standardize_xform_ops:38 of
msgid ""
"The USD prim to standardize. Must be a valid prim that supports the "
"UsdGeom.Xformable schema (e.g., Xform, Mesh, Cube, etc.). Material and "
"Shader prims are not Xformable and will return False."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.standardize_xform_ops:41 of
msgid ""
"Optional translation vector (x, y, z) in local space. If provided, "
"overrides the prim's current translation. If None, preserves the current "
"local translation. Defaults to None."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.standardize_xform_ops:44 of
msgid ""
"Optional orientation quaternion (w, x, y, z) in local space. If provided,"
" overrides the prim's current orientation. If None, preserves the current"
" local orientation. Defaults to None."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.standardize_xform_ops:47 of
msgid ""
"Optional scale vector (x, y, z). If provided, overrides the prim's "
"current scale. If None, preserves the current scale (after unit "
"resolution) or uses (1, 1, 1) if no scale exists. Defaults to None."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.standardize_xform_ops:51 of
msgid ""
"True if the transform operations were successfully standardized. False if"
" the     prim is not Xformable (e.g., Material, Shader prims). The "
"function will log an     error message when returning False."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.standardize_xform_ops:54 of
msgid ""
"True if the transform operations were successfully standardized. False if"
" the"
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.standardize_xform_ops:54 of
msgid ""
"prim is not Xformable (e.g., Material, Shader prims). The function will "
"log an error message when returning False."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.standardize_xform_ops:58 of
msgid "If the prim is not valid (i.e., does not exist or is an invalid prim)."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.validate_standard_xform_ops:3 of
msgid ""
"This function checks if the transform operations on a prim are "
"standardized to the canonical form: [translate, orient, scale]."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.validate_standard_xform_ops:6 of
msgid "The USD prim to validate."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.resolve_prim_pose:5 of
msgid ""
"This function ignores scale and skew by orthonormalizing the "
"transformation matrix at the final step. However, if any ancestor prim in"
" the hierarchy has non-uniform scale, that scale will still affect the "
"resulting position and orientation of the prim (because it's baked into "
"the transform before scale removal)."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.resolve_prim_pose:11 of
msgid ""
"In other words: scale **is not removed hierarchically**. If you need "
"completely scale-free poses, you must walk the transform chain and strip "
"scale at each level. Please open an issue if you need this functionality."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.resolve_prim_pose:15 of
msgid "The USD prim to resolve the pose for."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.resolve_prim_pose:16 of
msgid ""
"The USD prim to compute the pose with respect to. Defaults to None, in "
"which case the world frame is used."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.resolve_prim_pose:19 of
msgid ""
"A tuple containing the position (as a 3D vector) and the quaternion "
"orientation in the (w, x, y, z) format."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.resolve_prim_pose:22 of
msgid "If the prim or ref prim is not valid."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.resolve_prim_scale:3 of
msgid ""
"At an attribute level, a USD prim's scale is a scaling transformation "
"applied to the prim with respect to its parent prim. This function "
"resolves the scale of the prim in the world frame, by computing the local"
" to world transform of the prim. This is equivalent to traversing up the "
"prim hierarchy and accounting for the rotations and scales of the prims."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.resolve_prim_scale:8 of
msgid ""
"For instance, if a prim has a scale of (1, 2, 3) and it is a child of a "
"prim with a scale of (4, 5, 6), then the scale of the prim in the world "
"frame is (4, 10, 18)."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.resolve_prim_scale:11 of
msgid "The USD prim to resolve the scale for."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.resolve_prim_scale:13 of
msgid "The scale of the prim in the x, y, and z directions in the world frame."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.resolve_prim_scale:15 of
msgid "If the prim is not valid."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.convert_world_pose_to_local:3 of
msgid ""
"This function takes a position and orientation in world space and "
"converts them to local space relative to the given reference prim. This "
"is useful when creating or positioning prims where you know the desired "
"world position but need to set local transform attributes relative to "
"another prim."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.convert_world_pose_to_local:7 of
msgid ""
"The conversion uses the standard USD transformation math: "
"``local_transform = world_transform * inverse(ref_world_transform)``"
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.convert_world_pose_to_local:11 of
msgid ""
"If the reference prim is the root prim (\"/\"), the position and "
"orientation are returned unchanged, as they are already effectively in "
"local/world space."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.convert_world_pose_to_local:14 of
msgid "The world-space position as (x, y, z)."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.convert_world_pose_to_local:15 of
msgid ""
"The world-space orientation as quaternion (w, x, y, z). If None, only "
"position is converted and None is returned for orientation."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.convert_world_pose_to_local:17 of
msgid ""
"The reference USD prim to compute the local transform relative to. If "
"this is the root prim (\"/\"), the world pose is returned unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.convert_world_pose_to_local:20 of
msgid ""
"- local_translation is a tuple of (x, y, z) in local space relative to "
"ref_prim - local_orientation is a tuple of (w, x, y, z) in local space "
"relative to ref_prim,   or None if no orientation was provided"
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.convert_world_pose_to_local:22 of
msgid ""
"local_translation is a tuple of (x, y, z) in local space relative to "
"ref_prim"
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.convert_world_pose_to_local:23 of
msgid ""
"local_orientation is a tuple of (w, x, y, z) in local space relative to "
"ref_prim, or None if no orientation was provided"
msgstr ""

#: isaaclab.sim.utils.transforms.convert_world_pose_to_local:27 of
msgid "If the reference prim is not a valid USD prim."
msgstr ""

